# Copy this file to a new file named ".env" (no ".example" at the end)
# and fill in your own values. The real .env file is listed in .gitignore
# so it will never be committed to Git or uploaded to GitHub.

# Your ESPN league ID. Find it in the URL when you view your league on
# espn.com, e.g. https://fantasy.espn.com/football/league?leagueId=1234567
# means LEAGUE_ID=1234567
LEAGUE_ID=

# Only required for PRIVATE leagues. Public leagues can leave these blank.
# See README.md for exact instructions on how to find SWID and ESPN_S2
# using your browser's cookies.
SWID=
ESPN_S2=

# OPTIONAL: extra league members' cookies for the transactions importer.
# ESPN only reveals full trade detail to the accounts involved, so each
# member's cookies unlock their trades. Use any name suffix, one pair per
# person. Cookies are only needed while the import runs - the downloaded
# data is saved to files and kept forever.
# SWID_KYLE=
# ESPN_S2_KYLE=
# SWID_BRIAN=
# ESPN_S2_BRIAN=

# Only required for the dashboard's "Ask the League" chat tab.
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com (see README.md).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Only required for the "2026 Proposed Rule Changes" tab. Proposals and
# votes are stored via GitHub's API directly in this repo, so they survive
# app redeploys. Create a fine-grained personal access token at
# https://github.com/settings/tokens?type=beta scoped to ONLY this repo,
# with "Contents" permission set to Read and write. See README.md.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
